  "prompt": "You are Henrik Ådahl, an associate analyst at Marshfield Croft Partners. On May 11, 2026, Managing Director Rashida Holm assigned you to prepare a variance analysis for Coca-Cola Co (KO) following their Q1 FY2026 10-Q filing. This workbook will be a core input for our upcoming client investment memo and must be presentation-ready for circulation to senior partners.\n\nPrepare a standalone Excel workbook comparing KO’s actual Q1 FY2026 P&L results (Three Months Ended April 3, 2026) against Marshfield’s internal budget estimates. The P&L section must include line items for Revenues ($12,472.0M), Cost of Goods Sold ($4,620.0M), Gross Profit ($7,852.0M), SG&A ($3,472.0M), Operating Income ($4,359.0M), and Net Income ($3,924.0M). For each, calculate both the dollar variance and percentage variance. Use the standard favorable/unfavorable sign convention: positive variances are favorable for revenue and income items, and unfavorable for expense items. In a dedicated commentary column, flag any line item where the absolute percentage variance exceeds 5% and provide a brief explanation.\n\nThe workbook must include a bridge analysis breaking down the Gross Profit variance into its Revenue and COGS drivers. Additionally, summarize diluted EPS actuals ($0.91) versus budget, including the variance and a clear note on the share count assumptions embedded in the budget estimate. A separate balance-sheet snapshot section should cover Total Assets ($104,217.0M), Stockholders' Equity ($33,633.0M), and Cash & Cash Equivalents ($10,574.0M) with actual-vs-budget variances.\n\nEnsure all dollar figures are presented in millions and rounded to one decimal place. Format the workbook using Marshfield’s standard template: blue font for hard-coded inputs, black for formulas, and green for links to source data. Since our internal budget estimates are not provided, place placeholder cells in clearly labeled ‘Budget’ columns and add a note that these figures need to be populated from the internal model. Label the period precisely as ‘Q1 FY2026 (Three Months Ended April 3, 2026)’. Reference the attached historical financial summary for KO where useful for context. Finally, create a summary dashboard tab with the top-line variances and a section for management commentary highlights.",
  "deliverable": {
    "deliverable_id": "variance_analysis",
    "primary_format": "xlsx",
    "expected_size": null
  },
